GTE constant-table high-half loads must be SIGNED (sar), not zero-extended.

44 sites load the second short of a static GTE-vector constant into a GTE
input register via `mov eax,[DAT_xxxx]; sar $0x10,%eax` (verified at
0x43cb29/0x43cb3f/0x43cb4c Get_Corner_Positions, 0x424f0b Update_Debris-
family, 0x42ad3b, 0x42de1a, and the FUN_00440bf4 wheel-anchor blocks).
Ghidra emitted raw subpieces `(int)DAT_xxxx._2_2_`; the mechanical subpiece
conversion (patch 010) rendered them as zero-extending `(unsigned short)`
reads.  Negative constants (corner tables 0x466a96+/0x466d4e+ hold x/z
components like -186/-450) became ~65350 in the GTE input -> corner and
wheel-anchor transforms were wrong wherever a negative component was loaded.
Visible effect: Get_Corner_Positions produced a degenerate corner array for
the airborne attract car (all four wheel anchors equal -> skidmark quads
collapsed to a point -> the cf49+ "shadow trapezoid" divergence vs the
reference).  Fix: signed (short) reads at all 44 sites, matching sar.

